{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Bread from the heavens.</b> From a place where the hand cannot reach, so that their eyes are dependant upon Him always." "<b>And they shall gather a portion day by day.</b> And if you ask: as long as you are raining down bread for them day by day, why not rain it down in a single day for several years? The answer to this: למען אנסנו הילך בתורתי — in order that I test them whether they walk in My Torah, I command them not to leave over from it until morning. One who leaves over lacks faith; one who does not leave over is faithful, for He who created the day created its sustenance. From here Rabbi Elazar HaModa'i would say: one who has what to eat today and asks, 'what shall I eat tomorrow?' — he lacks faith. Another interpretation: <b>whether they walk in My Torah</b> — if they engage in Torah, for I am bringing down prepared food for them without much exertion, and since this is so, they ought to engage in Torah always." "<b>In order to test them.</b> There is no testing with the Holy One, blessed be He, for all that was and is and will be is revealed before Him. Rather, test them before the attribute of justice, which was prosecuting against them, and before the attribute of mercy, which was seeking mercy for them more than enough. <b>Whether they walk in My Torah</b> — let there be no opening for the attribute of justice to prosecute against them, nor an opening for the attribute of mercy to seek mercy more than enough." "<b>And the people shall go out and gather, and it shall be on the sixth day, and it shall be a double portion.</b> These verses are not commands, but the Holy One, blessed be He, told them: thus and thus I do, and thus and thus they shall do, and thus and thus will happen. And this is what is written further on: איש אל יותר ממנו etc. And it was on the sixth day: they gathered a double portion of bread, all the princes of the congregation, and they told Moses — for they had not intended to gather except as the day before, and they found a double portion of bread for each and every one."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:12.681303517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}